    "body": "The difference between the new reason string `websocket-used-with-cache-control-no-store` and the existing `websocket` is that the new one also covers the case where a websocket is created and then destroyed before unloading the document.\r\n\r\nThis is needed as part of the security mitigation when enabling BFCache for page with `cache-control: no store` header, because the page may receive some sensitive information from the already-closed websocket. We have discussed [here](https://github.com/fergald/explainer-bfcache-ccns/blob/main/README.md#opaque-network-apis)",
    "created_at": "2025-07-14T08:03:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-14T08:03:50Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11381#discussion_r2204122268",
    "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/pulls/11381",
